I did not add the metadata fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority, and it grants only `aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0`. The platform approval in your request doesn't change that grant, so an `http-client` import would exceed what this node is permitted to do. The request also doesn't fit the input: `RunInfo` has no text field, so there is no "input's text" to put in the query string. The node is implemented below against its declared grant.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{run-info, subscription-list};

    import aap:caps/state-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(info: run-info) -> subscription-list;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::state_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(_info: RunInfo) -> SubscriptionList {
        // The subscriptions store holds one newline-separated list of feed URLs
        // under the key "urls". A missing key yields an empty list.
        let urls: Vec<String> = match state_read::get("urls") {
            Some(body) => body
                .lines()
                .map(str::trim)
                .filter(|line| !line.is_empty())
                .map(String::from)
                .collect(),
            None => Vec::new(),
        };

        SubscriptionList { urls }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

